6. IMPORTANT SCROLL TRANSFORMATION
====================================================

This is one of the most important requirements.

The website should NOT simply show static sections when scrolling.

Scrolling should control the story.

When the visitor scrolls from the hero toward the About section, the developer character should smoothly transition from:

"welcoming / waving mode"

into:

"working / coding mode".

For example:

Hero:

Character smiles and waves.

As the user scrolls:

- camera slowly shifts
- character moves toward a workstation
- laptop/monitor becomes visible
- character sits or leans toward the workstation
- hand moves toward keyboard
- screen lights up
- code appears on the screen
- floating UI panels activate
- environment transforms into a developer workspace

The transition must feel continuous.

DO NOT simply fade one character image into another.

Create the illusion that the same character is changing state.

The animation should be controlled using GSAP ScrollTrigger or an equivalent scroll-driven animation system.

Scrolling down should progressively control the animation.

Scrolling back upward should reverse the animation smoothly.

